{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "04", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "17", "M": "54", "S": "00"}}, "news": [{"title": "Patna civic body to hold property tax camps across wards", "para": "Starting October 5, Patna Municipal Corporation will host ward-specific property tax assessment camps. These sessions aim to evaluate unassessed holdings and rectify the tax records. Homeowners are encouraged to attend to clear any outstanding dues and avert potential penalties. This initiative is part of an extended door-to-door survey designed to boost revenue collection, with sanitation inspectors earmarking properties for assessment.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/patna-civic-body-to-hold-property-tax-camps-across-wards/134669720?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-61652/134669720.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Rajasthan government notifies rural land conversion rules, moves approvals online", "para": "Starting November 2, 2026, Rajasthan is set to launch new regulations for the conversion of agricultural land to non-agricultural purposes. Applications can be submitted via a centralized online portal for efficiency. The fee structure varies: residential units will cost Rs 2,000, while other types will attract a Rs 20,000 fee.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/technology/rajasthan-government-notifies-rural-land-conversion-rules-moves-approvals-online/134669698?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-128548/134669698.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "technology"}, {"title": "Visakhapatnam civic body to streamline building permissions, water supply connections", "para": "In a recent meeting, GVMC's chief city planner A Prabhakar Rao assured developers that the town planning department is actively resolving building permission issues. This includes streamlining the application process for greater efficiency. Superintending engineer Pallam Raju addressed water supply connection procedures, while developers voiced concerns that officials responded to, elaborating on regulations and timelines for future projects. GVMC is committed to providing ongoing support to builders and developers.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/visakhapatnam-civic-body-to-streamline-building-permissions-water-supply-connections/134669680?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-18410/134669680.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}